2026-09-26 03:52:10

-- the configured value --
cd ../../wt-media-cloud/web && npm run dev:desktop

-- where 'cd ../../wt-media-cloud/web' resolves from each candidate cwd --
  cwd=/Users/aqiuye/Develop/workspace/wt-media/wt-media-desktop      -> MISSING
  cwd=/Users/aqiuye/Develop/workspace/wt-media/wt-media-desktop/src-tauri -> /Users/aqiuye/Develop/workspace/wt-media/wt-media-cloud/web

-- which cwd tauri actually uses (measured with a --config override that only prints pwd;
   no repo file was changed -- cargo tauri dev --config '{"build":{"beforeDevCommand":"pwd > /tmp/t05-tauri-cwd.txt && echo PROBE_OK"}}') --
  tauri beforeDevCommand cwd = /Users/aqiuye/Develop/workspace/wt-media/wt-media-desktop
  log:      Running BeforeDevCommand (`pwd > /tmp/t05-tauri-cwd.txt && echo PROBE_OK`)
  log: PROBE_OK
  log:         Warn Waiting for your frontend dev server to start on http://127.0.0.1:5174/...

=> tauri runs beforeDevCommand in wt-media-desktop, NOT in src-tauri.
   The configured 'cd ../../wt-media-cloud/web' therefore resolves to
   /Users/aqiuye/Develop/workspace/wt-media-cloud/web, which does not exist.
   From the measured cwd the correct form is 'cd ../wt-media-cloud/web'.
   One path segment too many -- a pre-existing defect in src-tauri/tauri.conf.json,
   not caused by this CHG (T-01 touched only the mode of bin/control.sh).

